# Stage 6 Traundl chain (D-077, D-085, D-087; game-design.md Stage 6
# section 5): the solver route to frame 2429 (swimming past the lantern
# pontoon, camera x 1967), then by hand: float until Traundl A comes back
# to its spawn end above her, jump out onto it (press 2615), ride A to its
# far end (2732), hop to the border raft (press 2735). Gelse #2 (col 154,
# row 6) hunts 2740-3220 and comes down on her on the raft (standing still
# it would reach her at 2819, 66 frames before B docks at 2885): a
# standing full jump (press 2794) stomps it. Hop onto Traundl B as it docks
# (press 2876), ride B to its far end, hop onto C (press 3010), ride C to
# its far-end berth (~3142), jump up onto the Zaunerstollen perch (press
# 3142, landing under the Z-box at 173). Gelse #3 (col 171, row 6, hunting
# 3102-3582) comes up to her on the perch; a standing full jump (press
# 3214) bumps the Z-box and stomps the Gelse on the way down; the
# Zaunerstollen lands on the perch short of the bollard (177), turns at its
# side and comes back to her: 1-up.
# Hand-measured press windows (only that press shifted, the rest
# unchanged; counted = she ends dry on the target / the Gelse is stomped):
# jump-out onto A 53 frames, A -> raft 45, Gelse #2 stomp >= 39 (every
# shift tried from landing on), raft -> B 48, B -> C 31, C -> perch 41,
# Gelse #3 stomp + box bump 8 (3211-3218).
# Gelse #3 never touches her during the C ride: standing on C at its far
# end she would first be reached at 3175 (wolfgangsee_gelse_c_berth), as
# C leaves the berth.
